{
    "background_story": "Jordan was a 19th-century fashion designer known for her exquisite creations. Among her most prized designs was a stunning pelisse, a luxurious silk coat with intricate embroidery and fur trim. The pelisse was commissioned by a wealthy socialite for a high-society ball, and Jordan poured her heart and soul into its creation. As the big night approached, Jordan worked tirelessly to ensure every detail was perfect. When the socialite wore the pelisse to the ball, she was the belle of the evening, with all eyes on her stunning coat. Jordan's pelisse became the talk of the town, and her reputation as a master designer was solidified. She went on to create many more breathtaking pieces, but the pelisse remained her crowning achievement, a testament to her skill and artistry.",
